values ('d2e3f4a5-6b7c-4d44-9e44-4f5a6b7c8d64', 'introduction-to-supply-chain-management', 'Introduction to Supply Chain Management', 'This course introduces supply chain management as the design and coordination of end-to-end flows of products, services, information, and money. Students learn how strategy, planning, sourcing, operations, logistics, inventory, technology, risk, and sustainability combine to create customer value. The syllabus is anchored in an introductory course block and strengthened with operations, procurement, logistics, inventory, demand planning, global supply chain, ERP, capstone, and engineering systems logistics support.');

