  'Introduction to Supply Chain Management',
  'This course introduces supply chain management as the design and coordination of end-to-end flows of products, services, information, and money. Students learn how strategy, planning, sourcing, operations, logistics, inventory, technology, risk, and sustainability combine to create customer value. The syllabus is anchored in an introductory course block and strengthened with operations, procurement, logistics, inventory, demand planning, global supply chain, ERP, capstone, and engineering systems logistics support.',
  $iscmjson${"slug": "introduction-to-supply-chain-management", "title": "Introduction to Supply Chain Management", "description": "This course introduces supply chain management as the design and coordination of end-to-end flows of products, services, information, and money. Students learn how strategy, planning, sourcing, operations, logistics, inventory, technology, risk, and sustainability combine to create customer value. The syllabus is anchored in an introductory course block and strengthened with operations, procurement, logistics, inventory, demand planning, global supply chain, ERP, capstone, and engineering systems logistics support.", "topics": [{"id": "0f20c1cd-8879-456a-8c78-6db09893ab01", "type": "topic", "title": "Supply Chain Strategy and End-to-End Value", "description": "Students begin by understanding the supply chain as a strategic system that links customers, products, suppliers, operations, logistics, information, money, and service outcomes.", "children": [{"id": "8f373f0a-14b2-4188-9d11-10f5dcc13347", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Supply chain purpose and competitive strategy", "children": [{"id": "0bb29d99-e8b1-4a85-8aa5-85f870f05e7f", "type": "concept", "title": "Cost, responsiveness, flexibility, innovation, quality, and sustainability priorities"}, {"id": "871432e2-cead-475a-b62b-0774dca903a6", "type": "concept", "title": "Strategic fit between customer needs, product type, and supply-chain capabilities"}, {"id": "603e1c65-8efb-453a-aade-d00f3a3195a7", "type": "concept", "title": "Tradeoffs between efficiency, speed, variety, reliability, and resilience"}], "description": "Students learn that supply chains are designed to support a chosen value proposition, not simply to move goods cheaply."}, {"id": "9a57944c-2dc7-440e-a975-07b3788e1b43", "type": "subtopic", "title": "End-to-end flows", "children": [{"id": "567d913c-bc59-41c9-a685-227b3a33e323", "type": "concept", "title": "Product, information, cash, and reverse flows"}, {"id": "9fde895d-26e1-4bfc-9fdc-f25b8fda8f67", "type": "concept", "title": "Suppliers, manufacturers, distributors, retailers, service providers, and customers"}, {"id": "efbdfae4-17f2-4978-8e91-233667e26ca4", "type": "concept", "title": "Interfaces, handoffs, delays, buffers, and coordination problems"}], "description": "A supply chain is a network of physical, information, and financial flows. Students learn to see how decisions in one function affect the whole system."}, {"id": "46e88707-2940-4fd0-bc43-3017fae56a58", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Value creation and value capture", "children": [{"id": "033a58a3-cf3f-47d4-9326-d42a1e915307", "type": "concept", "title": "Service, availability, lead time, customization, convenience, and reliability"}, {"id": "de6f5bcb-661a-4d29-aa85-12e1e366cb11", "type": "concept", "title": "Total landed cost, cash-to-cash cycle, inventory investment, and margin"}, {"id": "83f0e201-9622-4d2c-9711-dcdef1f208d3", "type": "concept", "title": "Supply chain as source of competitive advantage"}], "description": "Students connect supply-chain choices to customer value, revenue, margin, working capital, and risk."}]}, {"id": "fe1218f5-de0e-4940-834a-de58f7159504", "type": "topic", "title": "Plan-Source-Make-Deliver-Return Framework", "description": "This topic gives students a shared operating language for the major functions of a supply chain and how work flows across organizational boundaries.", "children": [{"id": "a14f40a2-c8e1-405d-955e-d0588170f889", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Planning processes", "children": [{"id": "b0bec0d6-7a03-4a56-a779-c95574a725bc", "type": "concept", "title": "Demand planning, supply planning, production planning, and financial alignment"}, {"id": "e21b372e-0fcb-42bc-b517-8890777ce098", "type": "concept", "title": "Aggregate planning, S&OP, service levels, and exception management"}, {"id": "a9ca26f1-58cc-44ad-b0c0-a65d72a3f32e", "type": "concept", "title": "Planning horizons: strategic, tactical, and operational"}], "description": "Planning converts demand, supply capacity, inventory, and business goals into coordinated decisions."}, {"id": "f1fca58b-ef07-49de-9ae6-281348b5827b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Source, make, and deliver", "children": [{"id": "9271a261-42e3-4ef1-9e39-567c4476e5f0", "type": "concept", "title": "Procurement, supplier management, manufacturing, assembly, and quality"}, {"id": "93447e61-c805-481f-891a-4b8fbd9716a3", "type": "concept", "title": "Warehousing, transportation, order management, distribution, and last mile"}, {"id": "0a35d6ce-048a-4834-87ba-fd9d8a79dcf6", "type": "concept", "title": "Make-to-stock, make-to-order, assemble-to-order, and engineer-to-order logic"}], "description": "Students learn the core operating functions that create and fulfill supply."}, {"id": "c17362a7-dd86-4c48-8b3f-e9db9ad298c8", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Return and reverse logistics", "children": [{"id": "e5a9ae84-ca98-4c8c-9cae-d417f83a0122", "type": "concept", "title": "Returns, repair, refurbishment, recycling, recalls, and disposal"}, {"id": "0fdc18bb-b634-437a-9f4f-cfcba7886f61", "type": "concept", "title": "Reverse logistics costs, customer experience, inspection, and disposition"}, {"id": "3c3845e9-07d3-4b26-b584-dae10d83d9ad", "type": "concept", "title": "Circular economy links to design, packaging, and product recovery"}], "description": "Reverse flows matter for service, sustainability, compliance, and profit recovery."}]}, {"id": "7cc98182-42ef-40df-b6e4-c12c6f6832db", "type": "topic", "title": "Process Mapping and Operations Foundations", "description": "Students learn how processes create flow, bottlenecks, waiting, cost, and quality outcomes before moving into supply-chain-specific decisions.", "children": [{"id": "bf20d716-52aa-47a9-a9c5-139487cf67eb", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Process analysis", "children": [{"id": "a951e2a7-3af9-4f5e-a655-a8b0e2b03c49", "type": "concept", "title": "Inputs, outputs, process steps, handoffs, queues, and decision points"}, {"id": "4b2f574f-8bd3-42d5-8ef0-89e81ba480ed", "type": "concept", "title": "Cycle time, takt time, throughput, work-in-process, and flow time"}, {"id": "941ba4be-48c9-4026-b937-1d8de3090779", "type": "concept", "title": "Value-added, non-value-added, rework, and waste"}], "description": "Students learn to map how work actually flows and identify where performance is created or lost."}, {"id": "92bdb6a5-b067-4b61-8058-cd9c8bb81c2c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Capacity and bottlenecks", "children": [{"id": "d223573f-cca8-4cd9-917f-4773f369c36f", "type": "concept", "title": "Capacity, utilization, bottleneck rate, throughput, and idle time"}, {"id": "f76f5ec3-0087-4f07-9747-7667004dcb47", "type": "concept", "title": "Theory of constraints and constraint elevation"}, {"id": "a8c9ff9b-1e36-4e14-a544-ebd8d3b9e88e", "type": "concept", "title": "Capacity cushions, flexibility, and demand variability"}], "description": "Supply chains are limited by constraints. Students learn to find and manage bottlenecks before adding resources blindly."}, {"id": "e45e2ac1-08cb-40d4-8f79-2f7a866593c7", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Lean and quality foundations", "children": [{"id": "7b60afe8-bbde-4b3d-b6b4-61de01663f5e", "type": "concept", "title": "Lean, waste reduction, standard work, visual management, and continuous improvement"}, {"id": "38e3b6eb-0622-47c7-9a57-1b78a25bee10", "type": "concept", "title": "TQM, Six Sigma, SPC, root cause analysis, and mistake-proofing"}, {"id": "4d65da41-4111-47b7-9835-2922e6ad8a03", "type": "concept", "title": "Quality at source and supplier quality links"}], "description": "Process improvement improves reliability, cost, and speed throughout the supply chain."}]}, {"id": "0d4f3ee7-c65b-4088-8359-878c093b96b8", "type": "topic", "title": "Customer Service, Demand, and Service Levels", "description": "This section connects supply-chain design to what customers actually experience: availability, speed, reliability, flexibility, and total value.", "children": [{"id": "6047ef04-b94a-445f-921e-7322047726a6", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Customer value and service design", "children": [{"id": "f93f688d-6a34-465a-84df-95262aabbe49", "type": "concept", "title": "Availability, fill rate, on-time delivery, order accuracy, lead time, and reliability"}, {"id": "889fc405-cb98-4b31-a612-271c465c8ade", "type": "concept", "title": "Customer segments, differentiated service, and channel expectations"}, {"id": "b10e6d53-2002-4458-b69f-d9538b5c1d6d", "type": "concept", "title": "Cost-to-serve and profitable service design"}], "description": "Students define service in measurable supply-chain terms instead of vague satisfaction language."}, {"id": "1fdfe2c4-38f3-49ab-81c9-4419f675264c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Demand behavior", "children": [{"id": "06122c69-e2d7-47d2-a0cc-bdf814165774", "type": "concept", "title": "Trend, seasonality, life cycle, promotion, substitution, and intermittent demand"}, {"id": "5331cfac-ac43-4973-acb3-db2bd43d3075", "type": "concept", "title": "Demand variability, forecastability, and demand shaping"}, {"id": "db39f67f-4ddf-4f43-868b-a891124bf071", "type": "concept", "title": "Bullwhip effect and information distortion"}], "description": "Students learn why demand is uncertain and why supply chains must plan for patterns, not averages alone."}, {"id": "0cc4c7de-09a2-4ded-8845-f6d1a9039ae6", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Service level tradeoffs", "children": [{"id": "e1e51f5b-6758-4e6b-bd7d-244900992d05", "type": "concept", "title": "Cycle service level, fill rate, safety stock, and stockout costs"}, {"id": "99aa63d1-9619-47a6-9f93-3366a8464277", "type": "concept", "title": "Customer priority, criticality, margin, and substitution risk"}, {"id": "342b23bb-600b-47a2-9893-71e084c397dc", "type": "concept", "title": "Balancing availability, inventory, and responsiveness"}], "description": "Higher service usually costs more. Students learn to choose service levels deliberately."}]}, {"id": "72ed1a54-ffc4-449a-a875-2756a50e7e53", "type": "topic", "title": "Network Design and Distribution Structure", "description": "Students study how facility locations, flows, channels, warehouses, plants, suppliers, and customers shape cost, service, risk, and resilience.", "children": [{"id": "ab280c82-a944-44b5-b98e-51f25a4617de", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Network structure", "children": [{"id": "1878b69b-8d0a-4ce4-8cfd-7dddc171872b", "type": "concept", "title": "Plants, suppliers, DCs, cross-docks, stores, ports, and customer zones"}, {"id": "82966f91-cfb0-4b94-aa87-3342bbace9e3", "type": "concept", "title": "Centralized versus decentralized networks"}, {"id": "592500df-98e6-4e7d-a4e8-7fa70da97a44", "type": "concept", "title": "Hub-and-spoke, direct ship, pooling, postponement, and omnichannel networks"}], "description": "Students study how facilities, suppliers, warehouses, and customers form the physical architecture of a supply chain."}, {"id": "bb58d792-c0a3-489a-9772-0484675e5584", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Location and flow decisions", "children": [{"id": "dd5a7a89-8253-47de-8661-c6a33c0100c5", "type": "concept", "title": "Facility location, lane design, allocation, and flow balance"}, {"id": "f507e61f-ea1d-4000-9396-328510588b56", "type": "concept", "title": "Fixed cost, transportation cost, inventory cost, lead time, and service constraints"}, {"id": "430e3a5d-f93f-4385-89cb-927a5347d237", "type": "concept", "title": "Scenario analysis and sensitivity testing"}], "description": "Network design links geography with cost, service, tax, trade, labor, risk, and capacity."}, {"id": "ad01ddfd-0a76-47f5-87e2-6903f515166b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Channel and distribution choices", "children": [{"id": "d442da7e-9629-45f6-9843-12baabbc0ead", "type": "concept", "title": "Wholesale, retail, ecommerce, marketplace, direct-to-consumer, and B2B channels"}, {"id": "5d6106c9-18fd-4ae5-8b3b-ebdcac313785", "type": "concept", "title": "Drop shipping, store fulfillment, ship-from-store, pickup, and micro-fulfillment"}, {"id": "ddd504de-bd50-4898-9087-86a18f5374ac", "type": "concept", "title": "Channel conflict, channel inventory, and service promises"}], "description": "Distribution structure shapes customer experience and profitability."}]}, {"id": "cbd67f0b-40b6-4fca-b6b5-24598fca0e49", "type": "topic", "title": "Procurement, Sourcing, and Supplier Relationships", "description": "This unit introduces the strategic role of sourcing, supplier markets, contracts, negotiation, cost, quality, risk, and relationship management.", "children": [{"id": "715e1db6-afea-4ead-9e80-95c4a7023030", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Purchasing and sourcing process", "children": [{"id": "f8a15b84-f4c6-4061-9a25-ea4e6bfe049f", "type": "concept", "title": "Requisition, RFx, bid evaluation, purchase order, receipt, and payment"}, {"id": "a5552155-60a9-41c5-8074-7bdf45e459b0", "type": "concept", "title": "Spend analysis, category management, and supplier market analysis"}, {"id": "e616676d-7a7b-4276-abde-62ce4944686d", "type": "concept", "title": "Total cost of ownership and value beyond price"}], "description": "Students learn how organizations identify needs, analyze spend, select suppliers, and manage purchasing work."}, {"id": "6acbea52-769d-4102-91ae-9a8163a55e0a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Supplier selection and negotiation", "children": [{"id": "062b0696-edd4-4e77-aeb3-b980d1c9239b", "type": "concept", "title": "Supplier criteria, scorecards, audits, capability assessment, and references"}, {"id": "f10c2a0a-d9bd-46ca-a4b1-1548f8f828ac", "type": "concept", "title": "Cost analysis, should-cost, negotiation preparation, and BATNA"}, {"id": "1add5674-3719-4631-9d68-e1818f271c9e", "type": "concept", "title": "Contracts, service levels, incentives, penalties, and governance"}], "description": "Supplier decisions affect quality, cost, innovation, continuity, and risk."}, {"id": "96bae556-3d2f-4d8a-8d4b-c9596524b3b3", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Supplier relationship management", "children": [{"id": "de279748-2161-4cb8-93ff-d9c0f0ea9361", "type": "concept", "title": "Strategic, preferred, transactional, and bottleneck supplier categories"}, {"id": "25c8395c-e61a-4155-8bb7-71f91d041559", "type": "concept", "title": "Supplier performance, collaboration, development, and innovation"}, {"id": "c6e7c943-e9bc-4b05-8a85-96393894f781", "type": "concept", "title": "Ethical sourcing, traceability, due diligence, and supplier risk"}], "description": "Strong supply chains manage suppliers as partners and risks, not just vendors."}]}, {"id": "ced4a46e-cb4a-4a13-bf17-c53c831386be", "type": "topic", "title": "Logistics, Transportation, and Last Mile", "description": "Students learn how products move through modes, carriers, distribution networks, international lanes, and last-mile systems.", "children": [{"id": "18ff47eb-6d4f-4bec-81e9-090275231d34", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Transportation modes and carriers", "children": [{"id": "9db25fec-6162-4880-9156-9047fc7d2558", "type": "concept", "title": "Truckload, LTL, rail, ocean, air, parcel, intermodal, and pipeline"}, {"id": "158c66db-b3de-428f-870f-eccb05f87a14", "type": "concept", "title": "Carrier selection, rate structures, accessorials, contracts, and service levels"}, {"id": "acf3f504-e9cd-42d5-b835-a8bb4314a77f", "type": "concept", "title": "Freight consolidation, mode conversion, and carrier scorecards"}], "description": "Students compare transportation options by cost, speed, reliability, capacity, emissions, and service fit."}, {"id": "4a9d6786-1ebb-40b8-9486-4b2d188ee325", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Routing, scheduling, and distribution", "children": [{"id": "e27afc16-6177-4156-8061-4d1b448931da", "type": "concept", "title": "Routing, dispatching, load planning, appointment scheduling, and dock management"}, {"id": "b54f9c60-8e2c-4f46-967f-1f5eabda4aeb", "type": "concept", "title": "Distribution networks, cross-docking, milk runs, pooling, and zone skipping"}, {"id": "f89cbcb1-dae4-4d73-9a15-5acbca431d7d", "type": "concept", "title": "Transportation management systems and freight visibility"}], "description": "Logistics decisions determine how goods move through a network day by day."}, {"id": "5761c545-fbac-494c-93f5-3ec4dfd113e9", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Last mile and international logistics", "children": [{"id": "c061e6d2-1356-4393-a0cf-d90996ba0ffe", "type": "concept", "title": "Last-mile density, delivery windows, returns, failed delivery, and customer communication"}, {"id": "e8d1cb12-f0ab-462f-8bda-03cf01e3019a", "type": "concept", "title": "Customs, duties, Incoterms, documentation, ports, and freight forwarders"}, {"id": "226a05e5-db65-4324-aad1-9318b1b9d200", "type": "concept", "title": "Compliance, security, congestion, and global lane risk"}], "description": "Students learn why last-mile and cross-border logistics are especially difficult and expensive."}]}, {"id": "43be7d30-4403-4cf8-8a02-1f76a6f1063b", "type": "topic", "title": "Inventory and Warehouse Management", "description": "This topic develops core inventory and warehousing decisions: how much to hold, where to hold it, and how to operate accurate, responsive facilities.", "children": [{"id": "96bdc5bb-8848-4d73-b540-ee76c03603e3", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Inventory fundamentals", "children": [{"id": "8f1e3997-0596-4cf4-b3ab-7ca60c051836", "type": "concept", "title": "Cycle stock, safety stock, pipeline stock, anticipation stock, and obsolete stock"}, {"id": "36153f91-5e60-4176-9e79-0e1c5feeec6e", "type": "concept", "title": "Holding, ordering, stockout, shrinkage, and obsolescence costs"}, {"id": "8bd6c9e4-4a0f-4163-8d23-153c8678a854", "type": "concept", "title": "EOQ, reorder point, order-up-to, min-max, and periodic review policies"}], "description": "Inventory buffers uncertainty but consumes cash and space. Students learn core policy logic."}, {"id": "832c36d7-3326-4129-9d57-a8007fc89d73", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Warehouse operations", "children": [{"id": "5092e48a-2cef-4a5b-b7a7-013394540528", "type": "concept", "title": "Receiving, putaway, storage, replenishment, picking, packing, shipping, and returns"}, {"id": "01e3cf0b-123b-47f3-94c6-e4fe8db11387", "type": "concept", "title": "Slotting, layout, labor planning, material handling, and automation"}, {"id": "00542057-f8ca-468e-88f5-bc615e525f35", "type": "concept", "title": "WMS, barcode, RFID, cycle counting, and inventory accuracy"}], "description": "Warehouses convert inventory into service. Students learn the work systems inside a facility."}, {"id": "37e0f846-a3ac-49cb-b24a-02e76ca91afa", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Inventory segmentation and control", "children": [{"id": "029edf1e-f46c-4733-895b-61ad593d335f", "type": "concept", "title": "ABC analysis, XYZ variability, criticality, margin, and service priority"}, {"id": "25a700e4-4c60-403e-9759-436458e995a5", "type": "concept", "title": "Slow movers, dead stock, substitutions, and lifecycle management"}, {"id": "71aab990-9c12-4026-9926-c730f105d6ab", "type": "concept", "title": "Inventory dashboards, exception reports, and root cause review"}], "description": "Different items need different rules. Students learn to segment inventory and manage exceptions."}]}, {"id": "8fee1390-49e4-4ce9-9e0c-5daeb5974563", "type": "topic", "title": "Forecasting, Demand Planning, and S&OP", "description": "Students learn how demand signals become plans and how organizations coordinate sales, operations, finance, supply, and executive choices.", "children": [{"id": "4927e624-367c-45db-858a-c1a185f499cd", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Forecasting methods", "children": [{"id": "d3bc6f83-a964-4012-9070-ce02a968603e", "type": "concept", "title": "Naive, moving average, exponential smoothing, trend, seasonality, and regression"}, {"id": "56d16fa5-e9ca-48be-9ebd-f7adb324ea02", "type": "concept", "title": "Forecast horizon, granularity, data cleaning, and new product forecasting"}, {"id": "93326de8-c3fd-40c2-a2f7-1249a1b00efd", "type": "concept", "title": "Bias, MAPE, MAE, RMSE, tracking signal, and forecast value added"}], "description": "Students learn practical forecasting tools and when each is appropriate."}, {"id": "a2faed62-1c67-4ca6-a4a5-6dfaec3267c5", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Demand planning process", "children": [{"id": "fc8380a5-d199-4f72-85ed-945898e4884d", "type": "concept", "title": "Baseline forecast, promotions, events, sales input, and consensus demand plan"}, {"id": "f9adf0ee-6e26-4417-97c9-b4d3e9c22c2d", "type": "concept", "title": "Demand sensing, exception management, and forecast collaboration"}, {"id": "09118767-8bcb-47d2-8e0d-5a0c2c93750f", "type": "concept", "title": "Demand shaping through price, promotion, allocation, and availability"}], "description": "Demand planning turns data and market knowledge into a forecast that the organization can use."}, {"id": "d62775aa-3e04-413e-81e0-e279cb141865", "type": "subtopic", "title": "S&OP and integrated planning", "children": [{"id": "309b847d-d336-43ac-9af1-ab6711b523e7", "type": "concept", "title": "Product review, demand review, supply review, reconciliation, and executive S&OP"}, {"id": "a84897cd-79aa-4049-8376-019664f84ec5", "type": "concept", "title": "Capacity constraints, inventory projections, scenarios, and financial implications"}, {"id": "6e71df0d-f265-4373-b579-20bc06db8bac", "type": "concept", "title": "Escalation, decision rights, and planning cadence"}], "description": "S&OP aligns demand, supply, finance, and leadership decisions."}]}, {"id": "7ac001a3-fef6-42e6-baf3-d0bd42c3d0a4", "type": "topic", "title": "Global Trade, Compliance, and Geopolitical Risk", "description": "This section expands the course globally: trade rules, customs, sourcing regions, currency, geopolitical shocks, and cross-border logistics all shape supply-chain performance.", "children": [{"id": "8538f8fc-ecf0-4c8d-a9dd-a694eac54fec", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Global sourcing and trade structure", "children": [{"id": "6d7878c1-9be5-4892-ab37-0aac28e572f2", "type": "concept", "title": "Labor, capability, cost, quality, market access, tax, and supplier ecosystems"}, {"id": "599726c4-de24-4418-a675-fa2e041359c8", "type": "concept", "title": "Nearshoring, offshoring, reshoring, friendshoring, and regionalization"}, {"id": "c3ce6a3b-5751-4460-812c-f45979903d1e", "type": "concept", "title": "Global network risk and multi-country scenario thinking"}], "description": "Students evaluate why firms source and produce globally and what tradeoffs follow."}, {"id": "d05d6f7a-8987-405d-a21c-4571a97e9a04", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Trade compliance and documentation", "children": [{"id": "328514bc-788d-496a-9fde-c9625a7d6aac", "type": "concept", "title": "Customs classification, valuation, rules of origin, licenses, and restricted parties"}, {"id": "91193006-508b-42be-a84a-0e71d929547a", "type": "concept", "title": "Incoterms, bills of lading, commercial invoices, packing lists, and certificates"}, {"id": "8b5c2cc1-abbc-4da9-836b-16a131011415", "type": "concept", "title": "Duties, tariffs, free trade agreements, and trade remedies"}], "description": "Cross-border flows require rules, paperwork, and compliance discipline."}, {"id": "87b6e0d7-6e48-40ec-9e7b-c92fd1ea3f97", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Geopolitical and macro risk", "children": [{"id": "e1a35b14-9a10-482b-8bf9-3b9e57588624", "type": "concept", "title": "War, sanctions, port disruption, pandemics, labor strikes, and natural disasters"}, {"id": "2fb90b93-dc66-4e03-a9e9-9ba0123b51e1", "type": "concept", "title": "Currency, inflation, energy, commodity, and interest-rate exposure"}, {"id": "6299d612-5de7-44c5-afc8-87232b58b965", "type": "concept", "title": "Country risk, supplier concentration, and contingency planning"}], "description": "Students learn to read external conditions as supply-chain variables."}]}, {"id": "96d5a86f-fd73-4017-9e16-3f5cee038780", "type": "topic", "title": "Supply Chain Information Systems, ERP, and Data", "description": "Students examine the systems and data that make supply chains visible, coordinated, and controllable, from ERP to planning systems and control towers.", "children": [{"id": "6b8cddab-ccd9-4e9c-b26c-cacf38df5583", "type": "subtopic", "title": "ERP and process integration", "children": [{"id": "c62169c0-dfbc-44e7-a005-ffcd94af0c9a", "type": "concept", "title": "Order-to-cash, procure-to-pay, plan-to-produce, and record-to-report"}, {"id": "5832b858-e9cb-4f72-a977-159096a1fb84", "type": "concept", "title": "Master data, bills of material, routings, suppliers, customers, items, and locations"}, {"id": "1736080b-832e-4dc0-89e3-eb922625e39c", "type": "concept", "title": "ERP configuration, controls, access, and implementation risk"}], "description": "ERP systems connect transactions across the supply chain. Students learn why process discipline and system design must match."}, {"id": "40b8e5f4-2889-4957-b975-ee962b0a8496", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Planning and execution systems", "children": [{"id": "ac88a279-45fd-421d-a7f8-00ea7a6491b7", "type": "concept", "title": "MRP, DRP, APS, WMS, TMS, SRM, OMS, and control towers"}, {"id": "8f8c3f27-9771-4f94-8b55-1ea5af727155", "type": "concept", "title": "Data flows between planning, execution, finance, and analytics"}, {"id": "739c0306-dfd9-48c3-87e7-816134b41f1f", "type": "concept", "title": "Dashboards, alerts, exceptions, and workflow automation"}], "description": "Different systems support planning, warehousing, transportation, sourcing, and visibility."}, {"id": "7e9e9b49-e887-4017-afc2-e461c4b80063", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Digital supply chain technologies", "children": [{"id": "35de1abe-96ae-4e31-a474-9bad0dbefa49", "type": "concept", "title": "IoT, RFID, barcode, robotics, AI, digital twins, blockchain, and analytics platforms"}, {"id": "d5625937-a447-42ec-92a8-a7880e09e922", "type": "concept", "title": "Use cases for visibility, predictive maintenance, ETA, quality, traceability, and planning"}, {"id": "73e331d9-b21e-46e4-89fe-a0f8c1c8ee1e", "type": "concept", "title": "Cybersecurity, data governance, internal controls, and adoption barriers"}], "description": "Students examine technologies that improve visibility, automation, and decision speed."}]}, {"id": "929b0072-e72c-4c12-b4a6-b7665667d723", "type": "topic", "title": "Metrics, Cost-Service Tradeoffs, and Analytics", "description": "This unit teaches students to measure supply chains with balanced metrics and use analytics to make tradeoffs rather than chase isolated performance numbers.", "children": [{"id": "fb2a043a-d949-4c6c-9fb3-05fd3b6813d2", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Balanced supply-chain scorecards", "children": [{"id": "d2cb9372-a200-4401-8f33-f6575d720dd5", "type": "concept", "title": "OTIF, fill rate, perfect order, lead time, inventory turns, forecast accuracy, and cash-to-cash"}, {"id": "7e2900e7-8510-4f8d-8937-9750817d8b9a", "type": "concept", "title": "Transportation cost, warehousing cost, procurement savings, quality, and supplier performance"}, {"id": "ce240a3f-7e73-433d-b63e-2d4efa795087", "type": "concept", "title": "Executive, functional, and operational metric layers"}], "description": "Students learn to measure performance across service, cost, asset, quality, risk, and sustainability."}, {"id": "b4ec8cf1-3a3c-4323-966a-dab3d4d88c75", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Cost-service tradeoffs", "children": [{"id": "ec7fa753-5398-418e-bfeb-b936e7200436", "type": "concept", "title": "Cost-to-serve, total landed cost, working capital, service level, and margin"}, {"id": "e501f828-c9e1-4b59-8f97-310c0b23922f", "type": "concept", "title": "Expediting, inventory buffers, transportation speed, and facility count"}, {"id": "ecd9d29a-c6b2-48c4-a440-faf6b4980754", "type": "concept", "title": "Sensitivity analysis and managerial decision thresholds"}], "description": "Supply-chain decisions usually improve one dimension while worsening another. Students learn to quantify tradeoffs."}, {"id": "e4b8782a-09e9-400d-bcc4-68b9da9a602a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Analytics for decisions", "children": [{"id": "809ba70a-c073-4b11-9c8b-6dddfbcbc344", "type": "concept", "title": "Descriptive, diagnostic, predictive, prescriptive, and causal analytics"}, {"id": "81562320-e73d-40ca-8d4f-cfa8f46dbea2", "type": "concept", "title": "Scenario analysis, optimization basics, simulation intuition, and decision trees"}, {"id": "b3b201d2-7963-4583-8752-6d5cfb6d08cf", "type": "concept", "title": "Translating analysis into recommendations and implementation plans"}], "description": "Analytics helps students move from reporting to better decisions."}]}, {"id": "20e495c8-b055-4daf-b10c-1702672d9514", "type": "topic", "title": "Risk, Resilience, and Continuity", "description": "Students learn to anticipate, map, absorb, and recover from disruptions while balancing efficiency with flexibility and redundancy.", "children": [{"id": "d634bab9-f95d-49d5-adde-c2d502cb9244", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Risk identification and mapping", "children": [{"id": "aa90f1cd-ed6a-4664-a49c-7648f1960241", "type": "concept", "title": "Supplier, facility, lane, country, capacity, quality, cyber, and demand risks"}, {"id": "3d0d79c0-c4f1-42c7-abaa-e038261b4c60", "type": "concept", "title": "Single points of failure, bottlenecks, geographic concentration, and hidden dependencies"}, {"id": "01469613-9671-4b50-b080-531adabcb1dd", "type": "concept", "title": "Risk heat maps, impact-likelihood scoring, and early warning indicators"}], "description": "Students learn to map vulnerabilities before disruption hits."}, {"id": "cee9f986-fc5e-42ce-b02c-1bf0d8ff9349", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Resilience design", "children": [{"id": "578bdad4-f780-490b-b9ff-86cd02ba1adc", "type": "concept", "title": "Redundancy, flexibility, postponement, dual sourcing, inventory buffers, and capacity options"}, {"id": "2a15ac94-f3ed-417d-baed-df692f0707e3", "type": "concept", "title": "Time to survive, time to recover, and recovery priorities"}, {"id": "15809449-c9cc-4e70-adfd-2d4a8a1d719d", "type": "concept", "title": "Tradeoffs between lean efficiency and resilient optionality"}], "description": "Resilience is designed through options, buffers, visibility, and relationships."}, {"id": "109a247b-5b48-4608-9e45-e6083eb2d9fa", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Continuity and response", "children": [{"id": "f55f532d-48b8-4fb0-b149-da94faa71c2c", "type": "concept", "title": "Business continuity plans, crisis teams, supplier communication, and customer allocation"}, {"id": "fac35773-9d36-49ba-a795-f81c975d4e03", "type": "concept", "title": "Disruption playbooks, scenario drills, and decision rights"}, {"id": "efa86ca5-9956-4602-bffe-be1a07626a70", "type": "concept", "title": "Post-disruption learning and network redesign"}], "description": "Students learn the practical structure of disruption response."}]}, {"id": "7cdd2e75-ac3b-4c3f-a9ab-8767e4d59215", "type": "topic", "title": "Sustainability, Traceability, and Circular Supply Chains", "description": "This topic treats environmental and social responsibility as supply-chain design problems involving traceability, emissions, labor, waste, circularity, and supplier due diligence.", "children": [{"id": "484e2628-6271-46d8-be96-3ac54f3f0936", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Environmental sustainability", "children": [{"id": "181cdb16-8f51-449f-a85f-d58a8590583a", "type": "concept", "title": "Scope 1, 2, and 3 emissions; carbon accounting; and logistics emissions"}, {"id": "33a87e30-0382-4a83-9803-d78dbbb17cc7", "type": "concept", "title": "Sustainable packaging, modal shift, energy efficiency, and waste reduction"}, {"id": "0656570a-bb33-4b3d-9e9c-56caf338cb46", "type": "concept", "title": "Supplier environmental performance and lifecycle thinking"}], "description": "Students connect supply-chain design to emissions, energy, waste, packaging, and resource use."}, {"id": "60a64424-6bb2-4619-be0c-33404cb4e490", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Social responsibility and traceability", "children": [{"id": "67888f50-03f4-4958-a3d1-e9f0a06e84ee", "type": "concept", "title": "Labor standards, human rights, conflict minerals, forced labor, and safety"}, {"id": "c279be27-ba1d-4537-8d7a-abb95f47b558", "type": "concept", "title": "Supplier codes, audits, certifications, traceability, and due diligence"}, {"id": "b63206c0-273d-44d5-a073-b74833d71c76", "type": "concept", "title": "Tier-n visibility, supplier development, and remediation"}], "description": "Students learn that ethical supply chains require visibility and accountability across tiers."}, {"id": "5fc020d5-0b00-436f-8f7b-e4a4322e0800", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Circular supply chains", "children": [{"id": "1bae3c7d-6f9d-445e-aa47-e4ba74702f20", "type": "concept", "title": "Reuse, repair, remanufacturing, recycling, return loops, and reverse logistics"}, {"id": "cffbe75b-7cc0-4e26-a781-1737d3cb24f3", "type": "concept", "title": "Product design for circularity, take-back systems, and secondary markets"}, {"id": "79dcfa96-de9f-479b-86c9-85ecea75cc65", "type": "concept", "title": "Measuring circular performance and business model implications"}], "description": "Circularity changes product and network design."}]}, {"id": "90e46ef0-a578-4d34-b8bf-adda50d002a0", "type": "topic", "title": "Capstone: Integrated Supply Chain Design and Executive Recommendation", "description": "The course culminates in an end-to-end case where students diagnose a supply chain and recommend a coherent strategy across cost, service, risk, technology, and sustainability.", "children": [{"id": "637380a8-7664-4718-96ad-d9303e4c3b6e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Case diagnosis", "children": [{"id": "8289899e-4cc6-4587-abf7-88b1ab31083d", "type": "concept", "title": "Customer promise, network, suppliers, inventory, logistics, systems, and metrics"}, {"id": "849cf069-a0c2-4ab1-85f9-e959802ae1df", "type": "concept", "title": "Root causes, constraints, risks, and stakeholder requirements"}, {"id": "b8217f0b-a9e6-4827-b07a-6c3be8b4c67f", "type": "concept", "title": "Baseline performance and problem statement"}], "description": "Students start the capstone by diagnosing an end-to-end supply chain using the course's full toolkit."}, {"id": "e1a5a54b-fb78-43f0-931d-f3e77218e69a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Strategic alternatives", "children": [{"id": "51404f19-2faf-4777-a2e6-99e0eea37633", "type": "concept", "title": "Network redesign, sourcing changes, inventory policy, technology, sustainability, and resilience options"}, {"id": "c839a076-fe13-41f6-a0c5-aa4fe20fd613", "type": "concept", "title": "Cost, service, risk, feasibility, timeline, and organizational impact"}, {"id": "1f411f86-751f-4a4f-aad1-3a3a442608fe", "type": "concept", "title": "Scenario analysis, assumptions, and sensitivity checks"}], "description": "Students develop and compare realistic options rather than jumping to a favorite answer."}, {"id": "5412157b-56f1-4b05-a528-13062b03690b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Executive recommendation", "children": [{"id": "f90c620d-5018-4b22-b8b6-9b013a947088", "type": "concept", "title": "Clear recommendation, rationale, implementation roadmap, and expected benefits"}, {"id": "b2c86851-4f5f-4939-838b-194414f162cf", "type": "concept", "title": "KPIs, governance, risks, change management, and next steps"}, {"id": "ae2da90e-0564-472c-a41d-ef0a4eb77a26", "type": "concept", "title": "Executive memo, presentation, appendix, and defense of tradeoffs"}], "description": "The final deliverable trains students to communicate like supply-chain leaders."}]}], "dbBacked": true}$iscmjson$::jsonb,
  true,
  false,
  'course',
  'public'
where not exists (
  select 1 from public.learning_paths where slug = 'introduction-to-supply-chain-management'
);

update public.learning_paths
set
  title = 'Introduction to Supply Chain Management',
  goal = 'Introduction to Supply Chain Management',
  summary = 'This course introduces supply chain management as the design and coordination of end-to-end flows of products, services, information, and money. Students learn how strategy, planning, sourcing, operations, logistics, inventory, technology, risk, and sustainability combine to create customer value. The syllabus is anchored in an introductory course block and strengthened with operations, procurement, logistics, inventory, demand planning, global supply chain, ERP, capstone, and engineering systems logistics support.',
  data = $iscmjson${"slug": "introduction-to-supply-chain-management", "title": "Introduction to Supply Chain Management", "description": "This course introduces supply chain management as the design and coordination of end-to-end flows of products, services, information, and money. Students learn how strategy, planning, sourcing, operations, logistics, inventory, technology, risk, and sustainability combine to create customer value. The syllabus is anchored in an introductory course block and strengthened with operations, procurement, logistics, inventory, demand planning, global supply chain, ERP, capstone, and engineering systems logistics support.", "topics": [{"id": "0f20c1cd-8879-456a-8c78-6db09893ab01", "type": "topic", "title": "Supply Chain Strategy and End-to-End Value", "description": "Students begin by understanding the supply chain as a strategic system that links customers, products, suppliers, operations, logistics, information, money, and service outcomes.", "children": [{"id": "8f373f0a-14b2-4188-9d11-10f5dcc13347", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Supply chain purpose and competitive strategy", "children": [{"id": "0bb29d99-e8b1-4a85-8aa5-85f870f05e7f", "type": "concept", "title": "Cost, responsiveness, flexibility, innovation, quality, and sustainability priorities"}, {"id": "871432e2-cead-475a-b62b-0774dca903a6", "type": "concept", "title": "Strategic fit between customer needs, product type, and supply-chain capabilities"}, {"id": "603e1c65-8efb-453a-aade-d00f3a3195a7", "type": "concept", "title": "Tradeoffs between efficiency, speed, variety, reliability, and resilience"}], "description": "Students learn that supply chains are designed to support a chosen value proposition, not simply to move goods cheaply."}, {"id": "9a57944c-2dc7-440e-a975-07b3788e1b43", "type": "subtopic", "title": "End-to-end flows", "children": [{"id": "567d913c-bc59-41c9-a685-227b3a33e323", "type": "concept", "title": "Product, information, cash, and reverse flows"}, {"id": "9fde895d-26e1-4bfc-9fdc-f25b8fda8f67", "type": "concept", "title": "Suppliers, manufacturers, distributors, retailers, service providers, and customers"}, {"id": "efbdfae4-17f2-4978-8e91-233667e26ca4", "type": "concept", "title": "Interfaces, handoffs, delays, buffers, and coordination problems"}], "description": "A supply chain is a network of physical, information, and financial flows. Students learn to see how decisions in one function affect the whole system."}, {"id": "46e88707-2940-4fd0-bc43-3017fae56a58", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Value creation and value capture", "children": [{"id": "033a58a3-cf3f-47d4-9326-d42a1e915307", "type": "concept", "title": "Service, availability, lead time, customization, convenience, and reliability"}, {"id": "de6f5bcb-661a-4d29-aa85-12e1e366cb11", "type": "concept", "title": "Total landed cost, cash-to-cash cycle, inventory investment, and margin"}, {"id": "83f0e201-9622-4d2c-9711-dcdef1f208d3", "type": "concept", "title": "Supply chain as source of competitive advantage"}], "description": "Students connect supply-chain choices to customer value, revenue, margin, working capital, and risk."}]}, {"id": "fe1218f5-de0e-4940-834a-de58f7159504", "type": "topic", "title": "Plan-Source-Make-Deliver-Return Framework", "description": "This topic gives students a shared operating language for the major functions of a supply chain and how work flows across organizational boundaries.", "children": [{"id": "a14f40a2-c8e1-405d-955e-d0588170f889", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Planning processes", "children": [{"id": "b0bec0d6-7a03-4a56-a779-c95574a725bc", "type": "concept", "title": "Demand planning, supply planning, production planning, and financial alignment"}, {"id": "e21b372e-0fcb-42bc-b517-8890777ce098", "type": "concept", "title": "Aggregate planning, S&OP, service levels, and exception management"}, {"id": "a9ca26f1-58cc-44ad-b0c0-a65d72a3f32e", "type": "concept", "title": "Planning horizons: strategic, tactical, and operational"}], "description": "Planning converts demand, supply capacity, inventory, and business goals into coordinated decisions."}, {"id": "f1fca58b-ef07-49de-9ae6-281348b5827b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Source, make, and deliver", "children": [{"id": "9271a261-42e3-4ef1-9e39-567c4476e5f0", "type": "concept", "title": "Procurement, supplier management, manufacturing, assembly, and quality"}, {"id": "93447e61-c805-481f-891a-4b8fbd9716a3", "type": "concept", "title": "Warehousing, transportation, order management, distribution, and last mile"}, {"id": "0a35d6ce-048a-4834-87ba-fd9d8a79dcf6", "type": "concept", "title": "Make-to-stock, make-to-order, assemble-to-order, and engineer-to-order logic"}], "description": "Students learn the core operating functions that create and fulfill supply."}, {"id": "c17362a7-dd86-4c48-8b3f-e9db9ad298c8", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Return and reverse logistics", "children": [{"id": "e5a9ae84-ca98-4c8c-9cae-d417f83a0122", "type": "concept", "title": "Returns, repair, refurbishment, recycling, recalls, and disposal"}, {"id": "0fdc18bb-b634-437a-9f4f-cfcba7886f61", "type": "concept", "title": "Reverse logistics costs, customer experience, inspection, and disposition"}, {"id": "3c3845e9-07d3-4b26-b584-dae10d83d9ad", "type": "concept", "title": "Circular economy links to design, packaging, and product recovery"}], "description": "Reverse flows matter for service, sustainability, compliance, and profit recovery."}]}, {"id": "7cc98182-42ef-40df-b6e4-c12c6f6832db", "type": "topic", "title": "Process Mapping and Operations Foundations", "description": "Students learn how processes create flow, bottlenecks, waiting, cost, and quality outcomes before moving into supply-chain-specific decisions.", "children": [{"id": "bf20d716-52aa-47a9-a9c5-139487cf67eb", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Process analysis", "children": [{"id": "a951e2a7-3af9-4f5e-a655-a8b0e2b03c49", "type": "concept", "title": "Inputs, outputs, process steps, handoffs, queues, and decision points"}, {"id": "4b2f574f-8bd3-42d5-8ef0-89e81ba480ed", "type": "concept", "title": "Cycle time, takt time, throughput, work-in-process, and flow time"}, {"id": "941ba4be-48c9-4026-b937-1d8de3090779", "type": "concept", "title": "Value-added, non-value-added, rework, and waste"}], "description": "Students learn to map how work actually flows and identify where performance is created or lost."}, {"id": "92bdb6a5-b067-4b61-8058-cd9c8bb81c2c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Capacity and bottlenecks", "children": [{"id": "d223573f-cca8-4cd9-917f-4773f369c36f", "type": "concept", "title": "Capacity, utilization, bottleneck rate, throughput, and idle time"}, {"id": "f76f5ec3-0087-4f07-9747-7667004dcb47", "type": "concept", "title": "Theory of constraints and constraint elevation"}, {"id": "a8c9ff9b-1e36-4e14-a544-ebd8d3b9e88e", "type": "concept", "title": "Capacity cushions, flexibility, and demand variability"}], "description": "Supply chains are limited by constraints. Students learn to find and manage bottlenecks before adding resources blindly."}, {"id": "e45e2ac1-08cb-40d4-8f79-2f7a866593c7", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Lean and quality foundations", "children": [{"id": "7b60afe8-bbde-4b3d-b6b4-61de01663f5e", "type": "concept", "title": "Lean, waste reduction, standard work, visual management, and continuous improvement"}, {"id": "38e3b6eb-0622-47c7-9a57-1b78a25bee10", "type": "concept", "title": "TQM, Six Sigma, SPC, root cause analysis, and mistake-proofing"}, {"id": "4d65da41-4111-47b7-9835-2922e6ad8a03", "type": "concept", "title": "Quality at source and supplier quality links"}], "description": "Process improvement improves reliability, cost, and speed throughout the supply chain."}]}, {"id": "0d4f3ee7-c65b-4088-8359-878c093b96b8", "type": "topic", "title": "Customer Service, Demand, and Service Levels", "description": "This section connects supply-chain design to what customers actually experience: availability, speed, reliability, flexibility, and total value.", "children": [{"id": "6047ef04-b94a-445f-921e-7322047726a6", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Customer value and service design", "children": [{"id": "f93f688d-6a34-465a-84df-95262aabbe49", "type": "concept", "title": "Availability, fill rate, on-time delivery, order accuracy, lead time, and reliability"}, {"id": "889fc405-cb98-4b31-a612-271c465c8ade", "type": "concept", "title": "Customer segments, differentiated service, and channel expectations"}, {"id": "b10e6d53-2002-4458-b69f-d9538b5c1d6d", "type": "concept", "title": "Cost-to-serve and profitable service design"}], "description": "Students define service in measurable supply-chain terms instead of vague satisfaction language."}, {"id": "1fdfe2c4-38f3-49ab-81c9-4419f675264c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Demand behavior", "children": [{"id": "06122c69-e2d7-47d2-a0cc-bdf814165774", "type": "concept", "title": "Trend, seasonality, life cycle, promotion, substitution, and intermittent demand"}, {"id": "5331cfac-ac43-4973-acb3-db2bd43d3075", "type": "concept", "title": "Demand variability, forecastability, and demand shaping"}, {"id": "db39f67f-4ddf-4f43-868b-a891124bf071", "type": "concept", "title": "Bullwhip effect and information distortion"}], "description": "Students learn why demand is uncertain and why supply chains must plan for patterns, not averages alone."}, {"id": "0cc4c7de-09a2-4ded-8845-f6d1a9039ae6", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Service level tradeoffs", "children": [{"id": "e1e51f5b-6758-4e6b-bd7d-244900992d05", "type": "concept", "title": "Cycle service level, fill rate, safety stock, and stockout costs"}, {"id": "99aa63d1-9619-47a6-9f93-3366a8464277", "type": "concept", "title": "Customer priority, criticality, margin, and substitution risk"}, {"id": "342b23bb-600b-47a2-9893-71e084c397dc", "type": "concept", "title": "Balancing availability, inventory, and responsiveness"}], "description": "Higher service usually costs more. Students learn to choose service levels deliberately."}]}, {"id": "72ed1a54-ffc4-449a-a875-2756a50e7e53", "type": "topic", "title": "Network Design and Distribution Structure", "description": "Students study how facility locations, flows, channels, warehouses, plants, suppliers, and customers shape cost, service, risk, and resilience.", "children": [{"id": "ab280c82-a944-44b5-b98e-51f25a4617de", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Network structure", "children": [{"id": "1878b69b-8d0a-4ce4-8cfd-7dddc171872b", "type": "concept", "title": "Plants, suppliers, DCs, cross-docks, stores, ports, and customer zones"}, {"id": "82966f91-cfb0-4b94-aa87-3342bbace9e3", "type": "concept", "title": "Centralized versus decentralized networks"}, {"id": "592500df-98e6-4e7d-a4e8-7fa70da97a44", "type": "concept", "title": "Hub-and-spoke, direct ship, pooling, postponement, and omnichannel networks"}], "description": "Students study how facilities, suppliers, warehouses, and customers form the physical architecture of a supply chain."}, {"id": "bb58d792-c0a3-489a-9772-0484675e5584", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Location and flow decisions", "children": [{"id": "dd5a7a89-8253-47de-8661-c6a33c0100c5", "type": "concept", "title": "Facility location, lane design, allocation, and flow balance"}, {"id": "f507e61f-ea1d-4000-9396-328510588b56", "type": "concept", "title": "Fixed cost, transportation cost, inventory cost, lead time, and service constraints"}, {"id": "430e3a5d-f93f-4385-89cb-927a5347d237", "type": "concept", "title": "Scenario analysis and sensitivity testing"}], "description": "Network design links geography with cost, service, tax, trade, labor, risk, and capacity."}, {"id": "ad01ddfd-0a76-47f5-87e2-6903f515166b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Channel and distribution choices", "children": [{"id": "d442da7e-9629-45f6-9843-12baabbc0ead", "type": "concept", "title": "Wholesale, retail, ecommerce, marketplace, direct-to-consumer, and B2B channels"}, {"id": "5d6106c9-18fd-4ae5-8b3b-ebdcac313785", "type": "concept", "title": "Drop shipping, store fulfillment, ship-from-store, pickup, and micro-fulfillment"}, {"id": "ddd504de-bd50-4898-9087-86a18f5374ac", "type": "concept", "title": "Channel conflict, channel inventory, and service promises"}], "description": "Distribution structure shapes customer experience and profitability."}]}, {"id": "cbd67f0b-40b6-4fca-b6b5-24598fca0e49", "type": "topic", "title": "Procurement, Sourcing, and Supplier Relationships", "description": "This unit introduces the strategic role of sourcing, supplier markets, contracts, negotiation, cost, quality, risk, and relationship management.", "children": [{"id": "715e1db6-afea-4ead-9e80-95c4a7023030", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Purchasing and sourcing process", "children": [{"id": "f8a15b84-f4c6-4061-9a25-ea4e6bfe049f", "type": "concept", "title": "Requisition, RFx, bid evaluation, purchase order, receipt, and payment"}, {"id": "a5552155-60a9-41c5-8074-7bdf45e459b0", "type": "concept", "title": "Spend analysis, category management, and supplier market analysis"}, {"id": "e616676d-7a7b-4276-abde-62ce4944686d", "type": "concept", "title": "Total cost of ownership and value beyond price"}], "description": "Students learn how organizations identify needs, analyze spend, select suppliers, and manage purchasing work."}, {"id": "6acbea52-769d-4102-91ae-9a8163a55e0a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Supplier selection and negotiation", "children": [{"id": "062b0696-edd4-4e77-aeb3-b980d1c9239b", "type": "concept", "title": "Supplier criteria, scorecards, audits, capability assessment, and references"}, {"id": "f10c2a0a-d9bd-46ca-a4b1-1548f8f828ac", "type": "concept", "title": "Cost analysis, should-cost, negotiation preparation, and BATNA"}, {"id": "1add5674-3719-4631-9d68-e1818f271c9e", "type": "concept", "title": "Contracts, service levels, incentives, penalties, and governance"}], "description": "Supplier decisions affect quality, cost, innovation, continuity, and risk."}, {"id": "96bae556-3d2f-4d8a-8d4b-c9596524b3b3", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Supplier relationship management", "children": [{"id": "de279748-2161-4cb8-93ff-d9c0f0ea9361", "type": "concept", "title": "Strategic, preferred, transactional, and bottleneck supplier categories"}, {"id": "25c8395c-e61a-4155-8bb7-71f91d041559", "type": "concept", "title": "Supplier performance, collaboration, development, and innovation"}, {"id": "c6e7c943-e9bc-4b05-8a85-96393894f781", "type": "concept", "title": "Ethical sourcing, traceability, due diligence, and supplier risk"}], "description": "Strong supply chains manage suppliers as partners and risks, not just vendors."}]}, {"id": "ced4a46e-cb4a-4a13-bf17-c53c831386be", "type": "topic", "title": "Logistics, Transportation, and Last Mile", "description": "Students learn how products move through modes, carriers, distribution networks, international lanes, and last-mile systems.", "children": [{"id": "18ff47eb-6d4f-4bec-81e9-090275231d34", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Transportation modes and carriers", "children": [{"id": "9db25fec-6162-4880-9156-9047fc7d2558", "type": "concept", "title": "Truckload, LTL, rail, ocean, air, parcel, intermodal, and pipeline"}, {"id": "158c66db-b3de-428f-870f-eccb05f87a14", "type": "concept", "title": "Carrier selection, rate structures, accessorials, contracts, and service levels"}, {"id": "acf3f504-e9cd-42d5-b835-a8bb4314a77f", "type": "concept", "title": "Freight consolidation, mode conversion, and carrier scorecards"}], "description": "Students compare transportation options by cost, speed, reliability, capacity, emissions, and service fit."}, {"id": "4a9d6786-1ebb-40b8-9486-4b2d188ee325", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Routing, scheduling, and distribution", "children": [{"id": "e27afc16-6177-4156-8061-4d1b448931da", "type": "concept", "title": "Routing, dispatching, load planning, appointment scheduling, and dock management"}, {"id": "b54f9c60-8e2c-4f46-967f-1f5eabda4aeb", "type": "concept", "title": "Distribution networks, cross-docking, milk runs, pooling, and zone skipping"}, {"id": "f89cbcb1-dae4-4d73-9a15-5acbca431d7d", "type": "concept", "title": "Transportation management systems and freight visibility"}], "description": "Logistics decisions determine how goods move through a network day by day."}, {"id": "5761c545-fbac-494c-93f5-3ec4dfd113e9", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Last mile and international logistics", "children": [{"id": "c061e6d2-1356-4393-a0cf-d90996ba0ffe", "type": "concept", "title": "Last-mile density, delivery windows, returns, failed delivery, and customer communication"}, {"id": "e8d1cb12-f0ab-462f-8bda-03cf01e3019a", "type": "concept", "title": "Customs, duties, Incoterms, documentation, ports, and freight forwarders"}, {"id": "226a05e5-db65-4324-aad1-9318b1b9d200", "type": "concept", "title": "Compliance, security, congestion, and global lane risk"}], "description": "Students learn why last-mile and cross-border logistics are especially difficult and expensive."}]}, {"id": "43be7d30-4403-4cf8-8a02-1f76a6f1063b", "type": "topic", "title": "Inventory and Warehouse Management", "description": "This topic develops core inventory and warehousing decisions: how much to hold, where to hold it, and how to operate accurate, responsive facilities.", "children": [{"id": "96bdc5bb-8848-4d73-b540-ee76c03603e3", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Inventory fundamentals", "children": [{"id": "8f1e3997-0596-4cf4-b3ab-7ca60c051836", "type": "concept", "title": "Cycle stock, safety stock, pipeline stock, anticipation stock, and obsolete stock"}, {"id": "36153f91-5e60-4176-9e79-0e1c5feeec6e", "type": "concept", "title": "Holding, ordering, stockout, shrinkage, and obsolescence costs"}, {"id": "8bd6c9e4-4a0f-4163-8d23-153c8678a854", "type": "concept", "title": "EOQ, reorder point, order-up-to, min-max, and periodic review policies"}], "description": "Inventory buffers uncertainty but consumes cash and space. Students learn core policy logic."}, {"id": "832c36d7-3326-4129-9d57-a8007fc89d73", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Warehouse operations", "children": [{"id": "5092e48a-2cef-4a5b-b7a7-013394540528", "type": "concept", "title": "Receiving, putaway, storage, replenishment, picking, packing, shipping, and returns"}, {"id": "01e3cf0b-123b-47f3-94c6-e4fe8db11387", "type": "concept", "title": "Slotting, layout, labor planning, material handling, and automation"}, {"id": "00542057-f8ca-468e-88f5-bc615e525f35", "type": "concept", "title": "WMS, barcode, RFID, cycle counting, and inventory accuracy"}], "description": "Warehouses convert inventory into service. Students learn the work systems inside a facility."}, {"id": "37e0f846-a3ac-49cb-b24a-02e76ca91afa", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Inventory segmentation and control", "children": [{"id": "029edf1e-f46c-4733-895b-61ad593d335f", "type": "concept", "title": "ABC analysis, XYZ variability, criticality, margin, and service priority"}, {"id": "25a700e4-4c60-403e-9759-436458e995a5", "type": "concept", "title": "Slow movers, dead stock, substitutions, and lifecycle management"}, {"id": "71aab990-9c12-4026-9926-c730f105d6ab", "type": "concept", "title": "Inventory dashboards, exception reports, and root cause review"}], "description": "Different items need different rules. Students learn to segment inventory and manage exceptions."}]}, {"id": "8fee1390-49e4-4ce9-9e0c-5daeb5974563", "type": "topic", "title": "Forecasting, Demand Planning, and S&OP", "description": "Students learn how demand signals become plans and how organizations coordinate sales, operations, finance, supply, and executive choices.", "children": [{"id": "4927e624-367c-45db-858a-c1a185f499cd", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Forecasting methods", "children": [{"id": "d3bc6f83-a964-4012-9070-ce02a968603e", "type": "concept", "title": "Naive, moving average, exponential smoothing, trend, seasonality, and regression"}, {"id": "56d16fa5-e9ca-48be-9ebd-f7adb324ea02", "type": "concept", "title": "Forecast horizon, granularity, data cleaning, and new product forecasting"}, {"id": "93326de8-c3fd-40c2-a2f7-1249a1b00efd", "type": "concept", "title": "Bias, MAPE, MAE, RMSE, tracking signal, and forecast value added"}], "description": "Students learn practical forecasting tools and when each is appropriate."}, {"id": "a2faed62-1c67-4ca6-a4a5-6dfaec3267c5", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Demand planning process", "children": [{"id": "fc8380a5-d199-4f72-85ed-945898e4884d", "type": "concept", "title": "Baseline forecast, promotions, events, sales input, and consensus demand plan"}, {"id": "f9adf0ee-6e26-4417-97c9-b4d3e9c22c2d", "type": "concept", "title": "Demand sensing, exception management, and forecast collaboration"}, {"id": "09118767-8bcb-47d2-8e0d-5a0c2c93750f", "type": "concept", "title": "Demand shaping through price, promotion, allocation, and availability"}], "description": "Demand planning turns data and market knowledge into a forecast that the organization can use."}, {"id": "d62775aa-3e04-413e-81e0-e279cb141865", "type": "subtopic", "title": "S&OP and integrated planning", "children": [{"id": "309b847d-d336-43ac-9af1-ab6711b523e7", "type": "concept", "title": "Product review, demand review, supply review, reconciliation, and executive S&OP"}, {"id": "a84897cd-79aa-4049-8376-019664f84ec5", "type": "concept", "title": "Capacity constraints, inventory projections, scenarios, and financial implications"}, {"id": "6e71df0d-f265-4373-b579-20bc06db8bac", "type": "concept", "title": "Escalation, decision rights, and planning cadence"}], "description": "S&OP aligns demand, supply, finance, and leadership decisions."}]}, {"id": "7ac001a3-fef6-42e6-baf3-d0bd42c3d0a4", "type": "topic", "title": "Global Trade, Compliance, and Geopolitical Risk", "description": "This section expands the course globally: trade rules, customs, sourcing regions, currency, geopolitical shocks, and cross-border logistics all shape supply-chain performance.", "children": [{"id": "8538f8fc-ecf0-4c8d-a9dd-a694eac54fec", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Global sourcing and trade structure", "children": [{"id": "6d7878c1-9be5-4892-ab37-0aac28e572f2", "type": "concept", "title": "Labor, capability, cost, quality, market access, tax, and supplier ecosystems"}, {"id": "599726c4-de24-4418-a675-fa2e041359c8", "type": "concept", "title": "Nearshoring, offshoring, reshoring, friendshoring, and regionalization"}, {"id": "c3ce6a3b-5751-4460-812c-f45979903d1e", "type": "concept", "title": "Global network risk and multi-country scenario thinking"}], "description": "Students evaluate why firms source and produce globally and what tradeoffs follow."}, {"id": "d05d6f7a-8987-405d-a21c-4571a97e9a04", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Trade compliance and documentation", "children": [{"id": "328514bc-788d-496a-9fde-c9625a7d6aac", "type": "concept", "title": "Customs classification, valuation, rules of origin, licenses, and restricted parties"}, {"id": "91193006-508b-42be-a84a-0e71d929547a", "type": "concept", "title": "Incoterms, bills of lading, commercial invoices, packing lists, and certificates"}, {"id": "8b5c2cc1-abbc-4da9-836b-16a131011415", "type": "concept", "title": "Duties, tariffs, free trade agreements, and trade remedies"}], "description": "Cross-border flows require rules, paperwork, and compliance discipline."}, {"id": "87b6e0d7-6e48-40ec-9e7b-c92fd1ea3f97", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Geopolitical and macro risk", "children": [{"id": "e1a35b14-9a10-482b-8bf9-3b9e57588624", "type": "concept", "title": "War, sanctions, port disruption, pandemics, labor strikes, and natural disasters"}, {"id": "2fb90b93-dc66-4e03-a9e9-9ba0123b51e1", "type": "concept", "title": "Currency, inflation, energy, commodity, and interest-rate exposure"}, {"id": "6299d612-5de7-44c5-afc8-87232b58b965", "type": "concept", "title": "Country risk, supplier concentration, and contingency planning"}], "description": "Students learn to read external conditions as supply-chain variables."}]}, {"id": "96d5a86f-fd73-4017-9e16-3f5cee038780", "type": "topic", "title": "Supply Chain Information Systems, ERP, and Data", "description": "Students examine the systems and data that make supply chains visible, coordinated, and controllable, from ERP to planning systems and control towers.", "children": [{"id": "6b8cddab-ccd9-4e9c-b26c-cacf38df5583", "type": "subtopic", "title": "ERP and process integration", "children": [{"id": "c62169c0-dfbc-44e7-a005-ffcd94af0c9a", "type": "concept", "title": "Order-to-cash, procure-to-pay, plan-to-produce, and record-to-report"}, {"id": "5832b858-e9cb-4f72-a977-159096a1fb84", "type": "concept", "title": "Master data, bills of material, routings, suppliers, customers, items, and locations"}, {"id": "1736080b-832e-4dc0-89e3-eb922625e39c", "type": "concept", "title": "ERP configuration, controls, access, and implementation risk"}], "description": "ERP systems connect transactions across the supply chain. Students learn why process discipline and system design must match."}, {"id": "40b8e5f4-2889-4957-b975-ee962b0a8496", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Planning and execution systems", "children": [{"id": "ac88a279-45fd-421d-a7f8-00ea7a6491b7", "type": "concept", "title": "MRP, DRP, APS, WMS, TMS, SRM, OMS, and control towers"}, {"id": "8f8c3f27-9771-4f94-8b55-1ea5af727155", "type": "concept", "title": "Data flows between planning, execution, finance, and analytics"}, {"id": "739c0306-dfd9-48c3-87e7-816134b41f1f", "type": "concept", "title": "Dashboards, alerts, exceptions, and workflow automation"}], "description": "Different systems support planning, warehousing, transportation, sourcing, and visibility."}, {"id": "7e9e9b49-e887-4017-afc2-e461c4b80063", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Digital supply chain technologies", "children": [{"id": "35de1abe-96ae-4e31-a474-9bad0dbefa49", "type": "concept", "title": "IoT, RFID, barcode, robotics, AI, digital twins, blockchain, and analytics platforms"}, {"id": "d5625937-a447-42ec-92a8-a7880e09e922", "type": "concept", "title": "Use cases for visibility, predictive maintenance, ETA, quality, traceability, and planning"}, {"id": "73e331d9-b21e-46e4-89fe-a0f8c1c8ee1e", "type": "concept", "title": "Cybersecurity, data governance, internal controls, and adoption barriers"}], "description": "Students examine technologies that improve visibility, automation, and decision speed."}]}, {"id": "929b0072-e72c-4c12-b4a6-b7665667d723", "type": "topic", "title": "Metrics, Cost-Service Tradeoffs, and Analytics", "description": "This unit teaches students to measure supply chains with balanced metrics and use analytics to make tradeoffs rather than chase isolated performance numbers.", "children": [{"id": "fb2a043a-d949-4c6c-9fb3-05fd3b6813d2", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Balanced supply-chain scorecards", "children": [{"id": "d2cb9372-a200-4401-8f33-f6575d720dd5", "type": "concept", "title": "OTIF, fill rate, perfect order, lead time, inventory turns, forecast accuracy, and cash-to-cash"}, {"id": "7e2900e7-8510-4f8d-8937-9750817d8b9a", "type": "concept", "title": "Transportation cost, warehousing cost, procurement savings, quality, and supplier performance"}, {"id": "ce240a3f-7e73-433d-b63e-2d4efa795087", "type": "concept", "title": "Executive, functional, and operational metric layers"}], "description": "Students learn to measure performance across service, cost, asset, quality, risk, and sustainability."}, {"id": "b4ec8cf1-3a3c-4323-966a-dab3d4d88c75", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Cost-service tradeoffs", "children": [{"id": "ec7fa753-5398-418e-bfeb-b936e7200436", "type": "concept", "title": "Cost-to-serve, total landed cost, working capital, service level, and margin"}, {"id": "e501f828-c9e1-4b59-8f97-310c0b23922f", "type": "concept", "title": "Expediting, inventory buffers, transportation speed, and facility count"}, {"id": "ecd9d29a-c6b2-48c4-a440-faf6b4980754", "type": "concept", "title": "Sensitivity analysis and managerial decision thresholds"}], "description": "Supply-chain decisions usually improve one dimension while worsening another. Students learn to quantify tradeoffs."}, {"id": "e4b8782a-09e9-400d-bcc4-68b9da9a602a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Analytics for decisions", "children": [{"id": "809ba70a-c073-4b11-9c8b-6dddfbcbc344", "type": "concept", "title": "Descriptive, diagnostic, predictive, prescriptive, and causal analytics"}, {"id": "81562320-e73d-40ca-8d4f-cfa8f46dbea2", "type": "concept", "title": "Scenario analysis, optimization basics, simulation intuition, and decision trees"}, {"id": "b3b201d2-7963-4583-8752-6d5cfb6d08cf", "type": "concept", "title": "Translating analysis into recommendations and implementation plans"}], "description": "Analytics helps students move from reporting to better decisions."}]}, {"id": "20e495c8-b055-4daf-b10c-1702672d9514", "type": "topic", "title": "Risk, Resilience, and Continuity", "description": "Students learn to anticipate, map, absorb, and recover from disruptions while balancing efficiency with flexibility and redundancy.", "children": [{"id": "d634bab9-f95d-49d5-adde-c2d502cb9244", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Risk identification and mapping", "children": [{"id": "aa90f1cd-ed6a-4664-a49c-7648f1960241", "type": "concept", "title": "Supplier, facility, lane, country, capacity, quality, cyber, and demand risks"}, {"id": "3d0d79c0-c4f1-42c7-abaa-e038261b4c60", "type": "concept", "title": "Single points of failure, bottlenecks, geographic concentration, and hidden dependencies"}, {"id": "01469613-9671-4b50-b080-531adabcb1dd", "type": "concept", "title": "Risk heat maps, impact-likelihood scoring, and early warning indicators"}], "description": "Students learn to map vulnerabilities before disruption hits."}, {"id": "cee9f986-fc5e-42ce-b02c-1bf0d8ff9349", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Resilience design", "children": [{"id": "578bdad4-f780-490b-b9ff-86cd02ba1adc", "type": "concept", "title": "Redundancy, flexibility, postponement, dual sourcing, inventory buffers, and capacity options"}, {"id": "2a15ac94-f3ed-417d-baed-df692f0707e3", "type": "concept", "title": "Time to survive, time to recover, and recovery priorities"}, {"id": "15809449-c9cc-4e70-adfd-2d4a8a1d719d", "type": "concept", "title": "Tradeoffs between lean efficiency and resilient optionality"}], "description": "Resilience is designed through options, buffers, visibility, and relationships."}, {"id": "109a247b-5b48-4608-9e45-e6083eb2d9fa", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Continuity and response", "children": [{"id": "f55f532d-48b8-4fb0-b149-da94faa71c2c", "type": "concept", "title": "Business continuity plans, crisis teams, supplier communication, and customer allocation"}, {"id": "fac35773-9d36-49ba-a795-f81c975d4e03", "type": "concept", "title": "Disruption playbooks, scenario drills, and decision rights"}, {"id": "efa86ca5-9956-4602-bffe-be1a07626a70", "type": "concept", "title": "Post-disruption learning and network redesign"}], "description": "Students learn the practical structure of disruption response."}]}, {"id": "7cdd2e75-ac3b-4c3f-a9ab-8767e4d59215", "type": "topic", "title": "Sustainability, Traceability, and Circular Supply Chains", "description": "This topic treats environmental and social responsibility as supply-chain design problems involving traceability, emissions, labor, waste, circularity, and supplier due diligence.", "children": [{"id": "484e2628-6271-46d8-be96-3ac54f3f0936", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Environmental sustainability", "children": [{"id": "181cdb16-8f51-449f-a85f-d58a8590583a", "type": "concept", "title": "Scope 1, 2, and 3 emissions; carbon accounting; and logistics emissions"}, {"id": "33a87e30-0382-4a83-9803-d78dbbb17cc7", "type": "concept", "title": "Sustainable packaging, modal shift, energy efficiency, and waste reduction"}, {"id": "0656570a-bb33-4b3d-9e9c-56caf338cb46", "type": "concept", "title": "Supplier environmental performance and lifecycle thinking"}], "description": "Students connect supply-chain design to emissions, energy, waste, packaging, and resource use."}, {"id": "60a64424-6bb2-4619-be0c-33404cb4e490", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Social responsibility and traceability", "children": [{"id": "67888f50-03f4-4958-a3d1-e9f0a06e84ee", "type": "concept", "title": "Labor standards, human rights, conflict minerals, forced labor, and safety"}, {"id": "c279be27-ba1d-4537-8d7a-abb95f47b558", "type": "concept", "title": "Supplier codes, audits, certifications, traceability, and due diligence"}, {"id": "b63206c0-273d-44d5-a073-b74833d71c76", "type": "concept", "title": "Tier-n visibility, supplier development, and remediation"}], "description": "Students learn that ethical supply chains require visibility and accountability across tiers."}, {"id": "5fc020d5-0b00-436f-8f7b-e4a4322e0800", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Circular supply chains", "children": [{"id": "1bae3c7d-6f9d-445e-aa47-e4ba74702f20", "type": "concept", "title": "Reuse, repair, remanufacturing, recycling, return loops, and reverse logistics"}, {"id": "cffbe75b-7cc0-4e26-a781-1737d3cb24f3", "type": "concept", "title": "Product design for circularity, take-back systems, and secondary markets"}, {"id": "79dcfa96-de9f-479b-86c9-85ecea75cc65", "type": "concept", "title": "Measuring circular performance and business model implications"}], "description": "Circularity changes product and network design."}]}, {"id": "90e46ef0-a578-4d34-b8bf-adda50d002a0", "type": "topic", "title": "Capstone: Integrated Supply Chain Design and Executive Recommendation", "description": "The course culminates in an end-to-end case where students diagnose a supply chain and recommend a coherent strategy across cost, service, risk, technology, and sustainability.", "children": [{"id": "637380a8-7664-4718-96ad-d9303e4c3b6e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Case diagnosis", "children": [{"id": "8289899e-4cc6-4587-abf7-88b1ab31083d", "type": "concept", "title": "Customer promise, network, suppliers, inventory, logistics, systems, and metrics"}, {"id": "849cf069-a0c2-4ab1-85f9-e959802ae1df", "type": "concept", "title": "Root causes, constraints, risks, and stakeholder requirements"}, {"id": "b8217f0b-a9e6-4827-b07a-6c3be8b4c67f", "type": "concept", "title": "Baseline performance and problem statement"}], "description": "Students start the capstone by diagnosing an end-to-end supply chain using the course's full toolkit."}, {"id": "e1a5a54b-fb78-43f0-931d-f3e77218e69a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Strategic alternatives", "children": [{"id": "51404f19-2faf-4777-a2e6-99e0eea37633", "type": "concept", "title": "Network redesign, sourcing changes, inventory policy, technology, sustainability, and resilience options"}, {"id": "c839a076-fe13-41f6-a0c5-aa4fe20fd613", "type": "concept", "title": "Cost, service, risk, feasibility, timeline, and organizational impact"}, {"id": "1f411f86-751f-4a4f-aad1-3a3a442608fe", "type": "concept", "title": "Scenario analysis, assumptions, and sensitivity checks"}], "description": "Students develop and compare realistic options rather than jumping to a favorite answer."}, {"id": "5412157b-56f1-4b05-a528-13062b03690b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Executive recommendation", "children": [{"id": "f90c620d-5018-4b22-b8b6-9b013a947088", "type": "concept", "title": "Clear recommendation, rationale, implementation roadmap, and expected benefits"}, {"id": "b2c86851-4f5f-4939-838b-194414f162cf", "type": "concept", "title": "KPIs, governance, risks, change management, and next steps"}, {"id": "ae2da90e-0564-472c-a41d-ef0a4eb77a26", "type": "concept", "title": "Executive memo, presentation, appendix, and defense of tradeoffs"}], "description": "The final deliverable trains students to communicate like supply-chain leaders."}]}], "dbBacked": true}$iscmjson$::jsonb,
